  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nRate of interest (r) = 4% per annum\n\nCompound Interest (CI) = ₹280.5\n\nTime (t) = 2 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nCI = P(1+(r)/(100))^t - P\n\nSI = (P×r×t)/(100)\n\n**Calculations:**\n\nCI = ₹280.5\n\n⇒ ₹280.5 = P(1+(4)/(100))² - P\n\n⇒ ₹280.5 = P(1.04)² - P\n\n⇒ ₹280.5 = P(1.0816 - 1)\n\n⇒ ₹280.5 = P × 0.0816\n\n⇒ P = ₹280.5 ÷ 0.0816\n\n⇒ P = ₹3437.5\n\nSI = (P×r×t)/(100)\n\n⇒ SI = (3437.5×4×2)/(100)\n\n⇒ SI = ₹275\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**\n\n6b:T67d,\n\n<",
